@koic 

Now there is an error. This should not lead to different results if `foo` is `nil`.

```ruby
2.7.6 :001 > foo = [1, 2, 3]
 => [1, 2, 3] 
2.7.6 :002 > foo&.map { |x| [x, x * 2] }.to_h
 => {1=>2, 2=>4, 3=>6} 
2.7.6 :003 > foo&.to_h { |x| [x, x * 2] }
 => {1=>2, 2=>4, 3=>6} 
```

```ruby
2.7.6 :005 > foo = nil
 => nil 
2.7.6 :006 > foo&.map { |x| [x, x * 2] }.to_h
 => {} 
2.7.6 :007 > foo&.to_h { |x| [x, x * 2] }
 => nil 
```
